# PX4 params for the raptor twin (sim). One file per vehicle: everything this vehicle always flies with. Mode overlays
# (ekf2_vision, ekf2_flow_range) are listed AFTER it in the scenario (`px4.params: [raptor, ekf2_vision]`, later wins).
# Format: NAME VALUE MAV_PARAM_TYPE (6 INT32, 9 REAL32). Names/ranges checked against the pinned PX4 tag (PX4_TAG, ADR-003).

# --- Collision prevention (Position mode): OFF on the raptor since 2026-10-22 ------------------------------------------
# Kinetix room scans fly close to the walls. PX4 v1.17 applies it in Position mode and to stick nudges in Auto modes, not to
# OFFBOARD setpoints. The ZED bridge still sends obstacle_distance (QGC proximity radar). iris.params keeps CP_DIST 1.5 for
# tests/collision_prevention.py (single_iris); set 1.5 here to bring it back on the raptor.
CP_DIST        -1.0 9   # m. Minimum distance PX4 keeps to an obstacle in Position mode; <= 0 turns collision prevention off
CP_DELAY       0.4  9   # s. Sensor + actuation delay PX4 allows for when braking
CP_GUIDE_ANG   30.0 9   # deg. Tolerance for slipping past an obstacle instead of stopping dead
CP_GO_NO_DATA  0    6   # 0 = allow flight where the map has no data; 1 = forbid it

# --- Rate loop: SIM ONLY. Never load these rows onto the real Pixracer (QGC) -------------------------------------------
# They fit the sim's placeholder plant (Pegasus' Iris thrust curve on the raptor's 0.8 kg / 7x smaller inertia / ~half
# arms), not the real 5" whoop; the real tune is Phase 4 (docs/todo.md). The gazebo-classic_iris gains limit-cycled on this
# body at takeoff (tests/hover_stability.py 2026-10-11: rate std roll 31 / pitch 106 / yaw 96 deg/s). Per unit of PX4 output
# the raptor gets ~2.5x the Iris' roll, ~3x pitch, ~6x yaw angular acceleration, so the Iris values (in the comment) are
# divided by about that: rate std 0.3 deg/s, attitude std < 0.1 deg (PASS).
MC_ROLLRATE_P   0.06    9   # 0.15
MC_ROLLRATE_I   0.08    9   # 0.2
MC_ROLLRATE_D   0.0012  9   # 0.003
MC_PITCHRATE_P  0.05    9   # 0.15
MC_PITCHRATE_I  0.067   9   # 0.2
MC_PITCHRATE_D  0.001   9   # 0.003
MC_YAWRATE_P    0.04    9   # 0.2
MC_YAWRATE_I    0.02    9   # 0.1

# --- Sensor positions (EKF2 lever arms), body FRD, m, from the CoM: the same on the Pixracer --------------------------
# Keep equal to the mounts in docker/sim/assets/vehicles/raptor/raptor.yaml (FLU there: FRD = [x, -y, -z]) and, for the camera, to
# `positional_tracking.initial_base_pose` in docker/zed/zed.yaml. EKF2 removes the rotation-induced motion of each sensor with these;
# they only act when that source is fused (ekf2_vio_flow_range, ekf2_flow_range).
EKF2_EV_POS_X   0.1205  9   # ZED Mini (zed_camera_link): FLU [0.1205, 0, 0.0527]. Centred on the real drone (forward offset only);
EKF2_EV_POS_Y   0.0     9   # hover-yaw-step fit over 20 sim flights: camera within 2 mm of these values (docs/vio.md)
EKF2_EV_POS_Z  -0.0527  9
EKF2_RNG_POS_X -0.0645  9   # LW20/C bottom face: FLU [-0.0645, 0.0011, -0.0353]
EKF2_RNG_POS_Y -0.0011  9
EKF2_RNG_POS_Z  0.0353  9
EKF2_OF_POS_X  -0.0645  9   # PMW3901: PLACEHOLDER, shares the LW20's spot (raptor.yaml)
EKF2_OF_POS_Y  -0.0011  9
EKF2_OF_POS_Z   0.0353  9
# Height of the body above the floor when landed, as EKF2 sees it (LW20 reading on the ground ~0.065 + EKF2_RNG_POS_Z). EKF2 uses this
# value in place of every INVALID range sample while landed and at rest. The default 0.01 told EKF2 the floor was 9 cm closer on each
# dropout (the twin: ~6 % of ground samples fall below its 5 cm minimum), and the sample at the takeoff transition left a 9-13 cm
# height offset for the whole flight (2026-10-15, docs/range-flow.md). Real drone: LW20 on the ground + RNG_POS_Z, measured.
EKF2_MIN_RNG    0.10    9
